; Off under sanitize and tsan, as the root dune says. The pages show what
; compiled calls report, so they run where rig links host code, on x86_64 and
; arm64, and where a clang is on PATH: a page cannot skip itself where its
; programs do not compile, as a test does. A clang older than tolk takes fails
; them, and a Clang that only CC names, as clang-16, leaves them out.

(mdx
 (package rune)
 (files
  index.md
  01-tracing.md
  02-derivatives.md
  03-maps.md
  04-loops.md
  05-totals.md
  06-compilation.md
  07-one-call.md
  08-callbacks.md)
 (enabled_if
  (and
   (<> %{profile} sanitize)
   (<> %{profile} tsan)
   (or
    (= %{architecture} amd64)
    (= %{architecture} arm64))
   %{bin-available:clang}))
 (libraries nx rune unix))
